# 🖼️ PCB Defect Detection Dataset (Created using Image Subtraction)

## 📌 About This Dataset  
This dataset was created by me as part of my work on **Printed Circuit Board (PCB) defect detection**.  
I started with two sets of images:  
- **Good PCB images** (without defects)  
- **Defective PCB images** (with defects)  

Using the **image subtraction method**, I subtracted the good PCB images from the defective PCB images.  
This subtraction clearly highlighted the defective regions, which I then saved as a new dataset.  

---

## 📂 Dataset Contents  
The dataset has three main parts:  
1. **Good PCB Images** – Clean PCBs with no issues  
2. **Defective PCB Images** – PCBs with different defects  
3. **Subtraction Results** – Highlighted defect regions after subtraction  

---

## ⚡ Defects Included  
The defective PCBs in my dataset contain the following categories:  

- 🕳️ **Missing Hole**  
- 🐭 **Mouse Bite**  
- 🔌 **Open Circuit**  
- ⚡ **Short Spur**  
- 🧩 **Spurious Copper**  

---

## 📊 How My Dataset Looks  
- Each defect type has its own folder.  
- Subtraction images clearly show the **difference between good and defective PCBs**.  
- Images are stored in `.png` and `.jpg` format.  

